{# The civic band: one line, one button, on every page, for something the
   town can act on by a date (civic.json). Rendered between the horizon
   and <main> by the base layout, and rendered as NOTHING when no notice is
   live, so the layout can carry it permanently.

   Not a ticker and not an alarm: no motion, no red, the site's own foam
   tint with a teal button, the same calm register as the safety notice
   on the Today board. Readers who have acted can close it with the ×,
   which is remembered in their browser for that notice's id only — a new
   notice shows again. The remembering is a per-reader convenience and
   nothing depends on it: with storage blocked, or JavaScript off, the
   band simply shows every time until it expires on its own.

   The script is the second inline script in the site and the smallest
   possible: it reads one key, hides one element, writes one key. #}
{% set civicLive = civic.notices | currentNotices %}
{% for n in civicLive %}
<div class="civic-band" id="civic-{{ n.id }}" role="region" aria-label="Notice">
  <div class="wrap civic-band-inner">
    <p class="civic-band-text"><strong>{{ n.text }}</strong>{% if n.detail %} <span class="civic-band-detail">{{ n.detail }}</span>{% endif %}</p>
    <a class="civic-band-btn" href="{{ n.href }}">{{ n.label }} →</a>
    <button class="civic-band-close" type="button" aria-label="Close this notice" data-civic="{{ n.id }}">×</button>
  </div>
</div>
<script>
(function () {
  var key = "civic-closed:{{ n.id }}", band = document.getElementById("civic-{{ n.id }}");
  if (!band) return;
  try { if (localStorage.getItem(key)) band.hidden = true; } catch (e) {}
  band.querySelector(".civic-band-close").addEventListener("click", function () {
    band.hidden = true;
    try { localStorage.setItem(key, "1"); } catch (e) {}
  });
})();
</script>
{% endfor %}
